WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:06.060
The mainline Conjuring movies may be coming to an&nbsp;
end — but could James Wan's horror universe live&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:10.140
on without them? The director has finally&nbsp;
addressed if the series has an afterlife.

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:15.660
Crafting a successful horror franchise&nbsp;
is no easy task, but James Wan has struck&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:20.640
gold with the Conjuring saga. These movies are&nbsp;
inspired by the cases of real-life paranormal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:25.560
investigators Ed and Lorraine Warren, who are&nbsp;
played by Patrick Wilson and Vera Farmiga,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:29.400
respectively. Of course, these chillers&nbsp;
might be somewhat questionable when it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:33.720
comes to their "true story" elements. However,&nbsp;
there is no denying their effectiveness as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:38.000
entertaining horror flicks. So, will&nbsp;
The Conjuring 4 continue that trend?

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:40.560
"Sometimes it's better to&nbsp;
keep the genie in the bottle."

00:00:41.129 --> 00:00:45.720
The first Conjuring movie tells the story of&nbsp;
a family whose rural farmhouse is haunted by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:50.220
a supernatural entity. The Warrens are called&nbsp;
in to solve the case, only to discover that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.220 --> 00:00:55.260
evil that dwells there isn't willing to go down&nbsp;
without a fight. The Conjuring 2 sees the Warrens&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.260 --> 00:01:00.000
traveling to London to help a single mother save&nbsp;
her children from an unwanted houseguest. Finally,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:04.320
The Conjuring 3: The Devil Made Me Do It&nbsp;
pits the paranormal investigators against the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:09.000
American legal system as they set out to prove&nbsp;
that demons inspired a man to commit murder.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:13.680
Every film in The Conjuring series has made&nbsp;
serious bank at the box office, and they've&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:18.600
been generally well-received by moviegoers too —&nbsp;
so Warner Bros. Pictures is undoubtedly interested&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:23.460
in making more. According to Wan, however, The&nbsp;
Conjuring 4 might be the saga's final entry.

00:01:23.460 --> 00:01:27.900
As it turns out, James Wan isn't interested in&nbsp;
producing more Conjuring sequels for the sake&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:31.980
of it. The filmmaker has too much respect for&nbsp;
the Warrens and the universe he's built around&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.980 --> 00:01:36.420
their cases to churn out mindless sequels.&nbsp;
During a recent interview with Collider,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:40.980
the horror maestro confirmed that The Conjuring&nbsp;
4 is still a work in progress and explained why&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.980 --> 00:01:44.880
he and his team aren't rushing to bring the&nbsp;
fourth installment to fruition. He said:

00:01:56.220 --> 00:02:00.420
It sounds like Wan and company are focused on&nbsp;
making a movie that lives up to the quality of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:04.800
its predecessors. However, while The Conjuring&nbsp;
4 might be the final movie in the main series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:08.220
it doesn't necessarily spell the&nbsp;
end of this cinematic universe.

00:02:08.220 --> 00:02:13.260
The Conjuring franchise has mastered the art of&nbsp;
the backdoor pilot, with the main movies featuring&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.260 --> 00:02:17.760
cameos from memorable spooks that then went on&nbsp;
to star in their own spin-off series. As such,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:21.660
the universe will likely live on in the&nbsp;
form of spin-offs after The Conjuring 4.

00:02:21.660 --> 00:02:26.760
For example, the Annabelle series has produced&nbsp;
three movies. Elsewhere, The Nun will unleash its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.760 --> 00:02:31.080
second installment later this year. It remains&nbsp;
to be seen if there will be a follow-up to The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:35.880
Curse of La Llorona, but that film grossed over&nbsp;
$100 million at the box office, so you can never&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:39.840
rule out the possibility. Unfortunately,&nbsp;
Wan's Crooked Man feature is apparently&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:44.640
no longer happening in its original form, but the&nbsp;
project may be revisited somewhere down the line.

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:49.140
Of course, The Conjuring 4 will undoubtedly&nbsp;
introduce another spooky entity that haunts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.140 --> 00:02:53.280
the nightmares of fans all around the world.&nbsp;
If that happens, who's to say that the demon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:56.580
in question won't be given the spin-off&nbsp;
treatment as well? The Conjuring movies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.580 --> 00:03:00.988
might well be one foot in the grave, but it&nbsp;
looks like there's life in the franchise yet.

